From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:46:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Build with the target interpreter

Build backends ran under sys.executable, the isolated environment hid
this process's system site directories, venv isolation cloned this
process's Python, and build requirements were installed by running pip's
source again with sys.executable. In the compiled kpip none of those
exist. Builds now run with the target interpreter -- what is built is for
it -- hiding its site directories; venv isolation has it create the
environment; and build requirements are installed by kpip itself
(own_command), told with --python which Python the environment is for.
With no Python at all, building is refused up front.
